Cyndy Fenninger is a partner at Orsbon & Fenninger, LLP. She is a member of the Estate Planning and Fiduciary Law sections of the American Bar Association and the Taxation section of the North Carolina Bar Association. She is a North Carolina State Bar certified specialist in Estate Planning and Probate Law.

Ms. Fenninger has extensive experience in a broad range of federal and state income, estate, and gift tax issues. She regularly advises and represents clients in the following areas:

Implementing sophisticated estate planning techniques to minimize the impact of estate inheritance, and income taxes on a decedent's estate, including charitable trusts, grantor retained trusts, qualified personal residence trusts and other tax-savings devices;

Creating living trusts to enable management and conservation of assets, enhance tax savings and avoid probate;

Establishing and implementing irrevocable life insurance trusts;

Handling estate administration matters with an emphasis on valuation issues;

Preparing of state and federal gift and estate tax returns and fiduciary income tax returns;

Advising fiduciaries concerning their powers and duties;

Coordinating retirement plan benefits in the estate planning setting; and

Gift planning to facilitate the transfer of assets during life at minimal gift tax cost and planning and carrying out a variety of tax-free reorganizations involving family.

